+      'A review shows what will happen in Intune for each app, which groups get it and anything to check, such as no groups or a second copy.',
+      'In the review, press Deploy now to start the deployment, or Change to fix an app first.',
+      'To change an app in the Deployment list, press its pencil button. Change it in Edit settings, then press Save to Deployment list. Clear list empties the list.',
+      'An app that is already in Intune is skipped. To deploy a new version or change it, open the app in Inventory or the App catalog and use Deploy again. It then shows Replaces current copy.',
+      'Add a second copy anyway adds the app to Intune again as a separate copy, marked Second copy. Afterwards, open Inventory and use Keep this copy to move the groups onto one copy.',
+      'Inventory may tag the older of the 2 copies Previous copy. IntuneGet never removes a copy you added on purpose, because the newer copy doesn\'t replace it.',
+      'Everything else is under More settings and What staff see during install. Each row shows its current setting, so you only open the ones you want to change.',
+      'To see where an app is deployed, open it in Inventory: Groups lists each group and whether it is Required or Available. No groups means it installs nowhere.',
+      'IntuneGet removes old copies left by its own updates (see How old copies are removed). For other copies, such as a second copy or one added in Intune by hand, use duplicate cleanup in Inventory.',
+      'If Inventory finds more than one copy of an app in Intune, it lists them at the top. Previous copies waiting for automatic removal are left out of that list.',
+      'Keep this copy moves every group onto that copy and leaves the others with none. Nothing is uninstalled.',
+      'Then Delete from Intune removes an emptied copy, which can\'t be undone. If another copy of the same app replaces it, that link is removed first. If a different app replaces or depends on it, the delete stops and says which app.',
+      'For an app that is already deployed, Save to Intune applies changes to groups, categories and When a new version comes out straight away.',
+      'Other changes, such as the version or New computer setup, need Deploy again. It replaces the current copy in Intune with the groups shown in the panel, rather than adding a second copy.',
+      'Required makes installation mandatory, with any postponement allowed by the package. Available lists the app in Company Portal for people to install themselves and works only with user groups.',
+      'Assign to a device group when every computer in the group needs the app, including shared computers and before anyone signs in.',
+      'Assign to a user group when the app follows the person to any computer they use, or when it is offered as Available.',
+      'Follow HRM\'s Entra group naming convention, and make it clear in the name whether a group holds computers or users.',
